Test Cases & Acceptance Criteria
Module 1: Registration
TC-REG-01: Successful User Registration

Given an unauthenticated user is on the Registration page,
When they fill in all required fields (e.g., name, valid email, strong password) with valid information and submit,
Then the account is created, a verification email is dispatched, and the user is redirected to the login or confirmation page.

TC-REG-02: Registration with Duplicate Email
Given an account already exists for user@example.com,
When a new user attempts to register using user@example.com,
Then the system blocks registration and displays an inline error indicating the email is already registered.

TC-REG-03: Input Validation for Weak Password
Given a user is on the Registration page,
When they enter a password that does not meet security criteria (e.g., under 8 characters, missing special characters),
Then submission is blocked and explicit error guidance is displayed under the password field.

Login & Logout
TC-LOG-01: Successful Login with Valid Credentials
Given a registered and active user is on the Login page,
When they enter their correct email and password and click "Log In",
Then they are authenticated, an active session/JWT token is created, and they are redirected to their designated landing page.

TC-LOG-02: Failed Login with Invalid Credentials
Given a user is on the Login page,
When they enter an incorrect email or password,
Then access is denied and a generic error message (e.g., "Invalid username or password") is shown without revealing which credential was incorrect.

TC-LOG-03: Login Attempt by Blocked/Deactivated Account
Given a user account status is set to "Blocked" by an Admin or Superadmin,
When the user enters valid credentials and submits,
Then authentication fails and the system displays an "Account is suspended or blocked" notification.

TC-LOG-04: Successful User Logout
Given an authenticated user is active in the system,
When they click the "Log Out" button,
Then their active session/token is invalidated, and they are redirected to the main public landing page.

TC-LOG-05: Back Navigation After Logout
Given a user has successfully logged out,
When they click the browser's "Back" button,
Then they cannot access protected pages,and the browser redirects them or prompts for re-authentication.

Set & Reset Password
TC-PWD-01: Request Password Reset Link
Given a registered user is on the "Forgot Password" page,
When they enter their registered email address and click "Send Link",
Then a unique, time-sensitive password reset link/token is generated and sent to their email.

TC-PWD-02: Successful Password Reset with Valid Token
Given a user receives a valid reset link and navigates to the Reset Password page,
When they enter a new password meeting policy requirements and confirm,
Then the password is updated in the database, the reset token is invalidated, and a success confirmation is displayed.

TC-PWD-03: Attempt Password Reset with Expired Token
Given a password reset token's expiration window (e.g., 15 minutes) has elapsed,
When the user clicks the link or submits a new password using the expired token,
Then the system rejects the operation and displays an error stating "Reset link has expired. Please request a new one."

TC-PWD-04: Attempt Password Reset with Reused / Already Consumed Token
Given a user has already successfully reset their password using token TOKEN_123,
When the user attempts to reuse TOKEN_123 via browser history or link re-entry,
Then the system rejects the token as invalid/consumed and prevents any password modification.

TC-PWD-05: Enforce Password History Rule (Same Password Attempt)
Given a user is resetting their password using a valid token,
When they enter their current/old password as the new password,

Then the system blocks the update and displays an error message (e.g., "New password cannot be the same as your previous password").
